  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 139 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nNorthwesterly flow is bringing a classic August fall teaser today, \nwith breezy winds, a broken altocumulus cloud deck, and dewpoints in \nthe 50s. Even lower dewpoints in the 40s are expected overnight into \nWednesday morning, which will likely make for a relatively chilly \nnight tonight. Expect overnight lows in the 40s for most, except \nright along Lake Superior. \n\nRinse and repeat tomorrow with a westerly breeze in the afternoon, \nlower dewpoints, and high temperatures in the 70s. \n\nA little wiggle in the upper level flow Thursday should allow for \nsome moisture and warmth advection back into the area, with \ndewpoints in the mid to upper 50s and temperatures rising into the \n80s. That impulse could also lead to some scattered showers and \nthunderstorms late Thursday through Friday. \n\nWe expect to stay under broad upper level troughing into next week \nwhich will keep us on the slightly cooler side. Any upper level \nshortwaves that move through could bring some passing precipitation \nchances.",
